# (after 0522) nvn/textures: the packaged-texture sharing table and the CPU-written texture tables are partitioned by pool (no more walks of millions of dead entries at each pool finalize)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/da242230e221aa533126577d555b62a3abc298ac  ("nvn/textures: partition packaged-texture and CPU-written tables by pool")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-22 22:11 +0800; Co-authored-by: Adam Durham
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: in long sessions mixing permanent and transient pools (Ocarina of Time over 140-200 area loads) g_pkg_share grew to hundreds of thousands of dead weak entries and
#   g_cpu_tex / g_cpu_tex_retired / g_cpu_unc to millions of retired ones (2.3 million after 160 loads), every slot walked under g_smu / g_cpu_tex_mu at each nvnMemoryPoolFinalize,
#   stalling tex_from_storage and every g_smu waiter (upstream issue #2507).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m, nvn_capture.inc, dm/gfx/README.md; new test t_pkg_share, t_cpu_tex pool_index, and test updates): g_pkg_share holds a map per pool (dead weak
#   references compacted before growing, capacity shrunk after spikes, a finalized pool's map dropped in O(1)); g_cpu_tex & co. become per-pool cpu_pool maps (g_cpu_pools) with a live
#   count; tex_cpu_written takes the texture (its pool's map).
# Adapted: 2 rejected hunks (tex_cpu_written(t->serial) callers) by hand; this tree's session reset (mtl_session_reset, t_session_reset) cleared the old global tables and now frees each
#   pool's map (pkg_share_pool_free, cpu_pool_free, written here; upstream has no session reset). The .github workflow hunk is not taken.
# Games: Ocarina of Time (long sessions); every game that finalizes pools. Switches: none.
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_pkg_share 13, t_cpu_tex 119, t_cpu_storage 143, t_linear_readback, t_read_owner 28, t_readback, t_session_reset 9; all in HOST_TESTS. NOT run on a device.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0522, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

